---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Android ADB device lane with REA 6.4+ | rea.run"
  description="Operator guide for REA’s Android ADB workflows: your device/emulator only — inspect, split-APK, logs, screenshots, lifecycle. No store-DRM framing."
  path="/docs/android-adb/"
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm"><a class="quiet-link" href="/faq/">← FAQ hub</a></p>
    <p class="badge badge-accent mt-4">Docs · 6.4+</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">Android ADB device lane (REA 6.4+)</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-4 !max-w-none">Use ADB against <strong>your</strong> device or emulator. This is an authorized-lab surface — not a guide to extract arbitrary Play Store DRM.</p>

    <h2>What 6.4 adds for operators</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Device inspect / split-APK handling / logs / screenshots / lifecycle hooks via the ADB lane.</li>
      <li>Apktool-oriented resource paths when those BYO tools are present.</li>
      <li>Pairs with existing JADX (BYO Java) static paths — confirm with <code>doctor</code>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Minimal hygiene</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Install platform-tools; confirm <code>adb devices</code> shows an authorized device/emulator you control.</li>
      <li>Pin <code>rea-agents@6.5.0</code> (or newer) and run provider/device doctor checks from upstream docs.</li>
      <li>Keep targets to apps you own, debug builds you built, or explicitly authorized fixtures.</li>
      <li>Prefer disposable emulators for untrusted APKs.</li>
    </ol>


    <h2 id="replace-650">6.5.0 install result fields</h2>
    <p>
      From <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.5.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rea-agents 6.5.0</a>, ADB install results require <code>replace_requested</code> to record whether <code>adb install -r</code> was requested.
      <code>replaced</code> is nullable because prior device package state was not observed. Do not treat reinstall intent as proof of replacement.
      Full break list: <a href="/docs/breaking/#nulls">upgrade runbook · 6.5.0</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/blog/rea-agents-6-4-0/">6.4.0 operator guide</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/jeb/">JEB, bring your own license</a></li>
      <li><a href="/showcase/aegis-totp/">Static APK study: authenticator login codes</a></li>
      <li><a href="/faq/what-can-i-analyze/">Capability matrix</a></li>
      <li><a href="/faq/legal-boundary/">Legal boundary</a></li>
    </ul>

    <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-[var(--color-line)] pt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] not-prose">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">Sources</p>
      <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-xs">
        <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.4.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rea-agents 6.4.0 release</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/android-analysis.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Upstream android analysis docs</a></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4"><a class="quiet-link" href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
